  "id": "DrugBank_DB01030 - MONDO_16248",
  "verbalization": "Topotecan is implicated in the pathogenesis of Familial Ovarian Cancer through a chain of indications that connect it to Ovarian Adenocarcinoma and then to Altretamine, which in turn links to Familial Ovarian Cancer. This suggests a potential role of Topotecan in the development of this condition, possibly through its effects on cancer cell proliferation or survival. The evidence is supported by multiple pathways, each linking Topotecan to a different cancer type, which may indicate a broader therapeutic profile or shared mechanisms of action. The presence of Altretamine in the chain, which is known to be associated with Familial Ovarian Cancer, further strengthens the hypothesis that Topotecan may influence the disease through a mechanism involving this drug. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility of a shared biological pathway or a role in the progression of ovarian cancer, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
